                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Not really for me. The platforming was clunky, the puzzles were brainless, the character movement felt like you were running through molasses and you had to actively fight the camera just to look around. It feels like I would've liked the game more if I watched someone playing it rather than actually playing it, which really is saying something.\r\nThe areas are beautiful but there's never anything to do so everything ends up just a superficial sightseeing tour that feels directionless most of the time.\r\nI also didn't empathize with the character at all because I didn't really see what was going on and the ending kinda felt tacked on, like the devs said \"Oh btw this thing was actually that thing, isn't that deep?\".",
